.\" karvi-sysutil(8): the administrator's tool for the service account's
.\" daemon. Written by hand; its rules are docs/EXAMPLES.md chapter 57's,
.\" issues 14 to 16, and its usage is the script's own (--help), so a change
.\" to the script changes this page.
.TH KARVI-SYSUTIL 8 "" "karvi"
.\" Paths and options are not hyphenated, and lines are not stretched.
.nh
.ds AD l
.ad l
.SH NAME
karvi\-sysutil \- set up or remove the service account's karvi daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sudo karvi\-sysutil daemon install
.RB [ "\-\-group \fINAME\fP" ]
.br
.B sudo karvi\-sysutil daemon remove
.RB [ \-\-purge ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B karvi\-sysutil
sets up a host's service account,
.BR karvi ,
whose daemon runs under systemd as the template unit's instance
.BR karvi\-daemon@karvi.service ,
started after the network, stopped before it at a shutdown, and bounded by
the daemon's grace alone. It runs as root, directly or through
.BR sudo ,
and exits 1 otherwise. An operator's own daemon, launched by the operator's
client, needs none of it.
.PP
.B daemon install
checks every refusal before it changes anything, then, in order: runs
.BR "karvi setup shared \-\-group" " \fINAME\fP,"
which reports each place
.B exists
on a host already set up; makes the system user
.B karvi
with its group, its home
.I /opt/karvi/users/karvi
(0750), which is also its private root, and no login shell, an existing
account of that name taken only when it is a system user with that home;
adds it to the operators' group,
.B netops
unless
.B \-\-group
names another; writes its configuration,
.I /opt/karvi/users/karvi/.config/karvi/config.toml
(0600, the account's), with
.BR "daemon.launch = \(dqsystemd\(dq" ,
under which no client of the account drains or starts a daemon; checks as
the account that karvi reads that value, which a global file setting
.B config.allow\-user\-layer = false
would prevent; enables and starts
.BR karvi\-daemon@karvi.service ;
and checks
.B karvi daemon status
as the account. Each part is reported
.BR created ,
.BR exists ,
or
.BR repaired ,
and entered in the record as it is made or found.
.PP
Run again,
.B daemon install
finishes an install that failed partway and, over a whole one, changes
nothing. It repairs what the record lists as made: a part missing is made
again, the account with its recorded uid, so that its files keep their
owner; the account's home and login shell, the owner and mode of its home
and of its configuration, and its group membership are set back; and the
instance is enabled and started when it is not. A repaired part's value as
found is shown over the value set. It never rewrites the configuration's
content, refusing a
.B daemon.launch
other than
.BR systemd ,
and never restarts a daemon of another build, which waits on the
administrator's
.BR "systemctl restart karvi\-daemon@karvi.service" .
.PP
.B daemon remove
undoes what the record lists as made, in reverse: it disables and stops the
instance, the stop waiting for the daemon's jobs under its grace as at a
shutdown, and removes the configuration file and the group membership. The
account and its home stay, so that its files keep their owner, and their
lines stay in the record; a later
.B daemon install
takes the account back.
.B \-\-purge
also gives every file the account owns in the shared trees and the shared
scratch to root, their group and mode unchanged, so that operators still
read them and no later account owns them, and removes the account and its
home and the record. What the install found is left, and so are the shared
trees, which hold every operator's work, and the template unit, which is the
package's. A part already gone is reported
.BR absent ;
without a record,
.B daemon remove
is refused.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-group " NAME"
The operators' group, which must exist:
.B karvi setup shared
makes the shared trees in it and the account joins it.
.B netops
when not given; an install whose record names another group is refused.
.TP
.B \-\-purge
With
.BR "daemon remove" :
remove the account and its home as well.
.TP
.B \-\-nocolor
No colour on standard error, which at a terminal shows errors in red and
warnings in orange, as karvi does;
.B NO_COLOR
set and not empty does the same.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
The usage.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/system/karvi\-daemon@.service
The package's template unit: nothing runs until an instance is enabled, and
an upgrade replaces it and reloads systemd. A site's own settings go in a
drop-in under
.IR /etc/systemd/system/karvi\-daemon@.service.d/ ,
which an upgrade never touches.
.TP
.I /etc/karvi/service\-karvi.installed
The record: the configuration the unit's daemon runs with, the global file
and then the account's own, and one line per part, made or found.
.TP
.I /opt/karvi/users/karvi/.config/karvi/config.toml
The account's configuration.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 when done; 1 for a refusal or a failure, nothing changed by a refusal; 2
for a usage error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR karvi\-daemon (1),
.BR karvi\-setup (1),
.BR systemctl (1),
.I /usr/share/doc/karvi/docs/OPERATIONS.md
